$DATUM Synthesis of (butylcarbamoyl)(thiophen-2-yl)methyl benzoate (30)
Following General Procedure II, a mixture of isocyanide 14 (40 mg, 41 μL,
0.48 mmol, 1.0 equiv), benzoic acid (5) (61.5 mg, 0.50 mmol, 1.05 equiv)
and aldehyde 12 (56 mg, 46 μL, 0.50 mmol, 1.05 equiv) in CH2Cl2 was
stirred for 48 hrs. After removal of solvent and silica gel
chromatography, 30 (116 mg, 76%) was obtained as a whitish-green solid.
Data for 30: 1H NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.12-8.08 (m, 2H, aryl);
7.63-7.58 (m, 1H, aryl); 7.50-7.42 (m, 2H, aryl); 7.33 (dd, J= 1.2, 5.2
Hz, 1H, aryl); 7.25 (d, J= 4.0 Hz, 1H, aryl); 7.00 (dd, J= 3.6, 5.2 Hz,
1H, aryl); 6.60 (s, 1H, CH); 6.27 (bt, 1H, NH); 3.40-3.26 (m, 2H, CH2);
1.55-1.47 (quint, J= 7.6 Hz, 2H, CH2); 1.37-1.29 (sext, J= 7.2 Hz, 2H,
CH2); 0.88 (t, J= 7.2 Hz, 3H, CH3) 13C NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.7,
165.1, 137.7, 134.0, 130.4, 130.2, 129.3, 128.8, 128.0, 127.1, 71.9,
39.6, 31.7, 20.2, 13.9 IR: (neat) νmax = 3300, 2958, 2932, 1725, 1664,
1543, 1451, 1264, 1107, 708 cm-1 TLC: Rf = 0.37 (EtOAc:Hex 1:2) LRMS:
EIMS calculated for C17H19NO3S+ [M+ H]+: 318.1, found: 317.1 HPLC:
(+/−)-30 tR 16.3 min (48.2%); tR 20.6 min (51.8 %) (−)-30 tR 16.8 min
(18.2%); tR 20.2 min (81.7%) (Diacel Chiralpak AS-H 0.46 cm φ x 25 cm,
Gradient; t10min 10% IPA in Hexane, t10min 12% IPA in Hexane, t20min 14%
IPA in Hexane, t50min 16% IPA in Hexane, t65min 20% IPA in Hexane, 1
mL/min) OR: [α]D22 = -5.6° (CHCl3, c = 0.95)
