$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of tricyclic lactone (33) Following General Procedure II, a
mixture of isocyanide 11 (27 mg, 28 μL, 0.23 mmol, 1.0 equiv), fumaric
acid monoethyl ester (32) (35 mg, 0.24 mmol, 1.05 equiv) and aldehyde 10
(23 mg, 20 μL, 0.24 mmol, 1.05 equiv) in CH2Cl2 was stirred 48 hrs. After
removal of solvent and silica gel chromatography, 33 (112 mg, 75%) was
obtained as a yellowish-brown oil which was a mixture of diastereomers in
15:1 ratio as noted by 1H NMR. The major diastereomer was isolated by
silica gel chromatography. Data for 33: 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.34-7.25 (m, 5H, aryl); 6.80 (d, J= 6.0 Hz, 1H, CH olefin); 6.77 (bt,
1H, NH); 6.40-6.39 (dd, J= 1.5, 5.0 Hz, 1H, CH olefin); 5.42 (s, 1H, CH);
5.35-5.34 (dd, J= 1.5, 4.5 Hz, 1H, CH oxygen bridge); 4.56-4.51 (dd, J=
6.5, 15.5 Hz, 1H, CH benzyl); 4.48-4.43 (dd, J= 6.0, 15.0 Hz, 1H, CH
benzyl); 4.16-4.12 (q, J= 7.0 Hz, 2H, CH2); 3.57-3.56 (dd, J= 3.0, 5.0
Hz, 1H, CH); 3.21 (d, J= 3.5 Hz, 1H, CH); 1.26 (t, J= 8.0 Hz, CH3) 13C
NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 174.3, 170.3, 166.9, 137.9, 135.2, 135.1, 134.4,
129.1, 129.0, 128.3, 128.2, 128.1, 128.0, 92.1, 80.4, 63.5, 61.5, 50.7,
47.3, 46.3, 44.0, 14.4 TLC: Rf = 0.37 (EtOAc:Hex 1:2) LRMS: EIMS
calculated for C19H19NO6+ [M+ H]+: 358.1, found: 358.0 HPLC: (+/−)-33 tR
25.2 min (47.9%); tR 29.8 min (52.1%) (Major diastereomer) 33 tR 26.7 min
(8.6%); tR 30.1 min (91.4%) (Diacel Chiralpak AS-H 0.46 cm φ x 25 cm,
Gradient; t00% IPA in Hexane, t10min 2% IPA in Hexane, t20min 4% IPA in
Hexane, t30min 6% IPA in Hexane, 1 mL/min)
