$DATUM 3-Benzyloxycarbonylamino-N-[1-(cyclohex-1-enylcarbamoyl)-cyclobutyl]-N-(2,4-dimethoxybenzyl)succinamic
Acid Benzyl Ester (13). Z-β-(Benzyl ester)-L-aspartic acid (36 mg, 0.10
mmol), 2,4-dimethoxybenzylamine (15 μL, 0.10 mmol), cyclobutanone (8.0
μL, 0.10 mmol), and 1-isocyanocyclohexene (0.10 mL of a 1 M solution in
pentane, 0.10 mmol) were dissolved in 1 mL of MeOH in a 10 mL
round-bottom flask with a stir bar. The reaction mixture was stirred at
room temperature overnight. The reaction mixture was concentrated in
vacuo. The product was purified by flash chromatography (ethyl
acetate/hexanes 1:2) to afford 13 as a white solid (51 mg, 75%). Rf =0.37
(ethyl acetate/hexanes 1:2). 1HNMR (CDCl3): δ 8.10 (s, 1H), 7.34 (m,
10H), 7.00 (d, J =8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.39 (dd, J =8.7, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 6.32 (d, J
=1.8 Hz, 1H), 5.11-5.75 (m, 2H), 5.11 (s, 2H), 5.07 (s, 2H), 4.53 (d, J
=15.9 Hz, 1H), 4.34 (d, J =16.5 Hz, 1H), 3.76 (s, 3H), 3.64 (s, 3H),
2.54-2.86 (m, 4H), 1.95-2.24 (m, 4H), 1.50-1.65 (m, 8H). 13C NMR (CDCl3):
δ 172.3, 170.7, 170.5, 161.1, 158.4, 155.5, 136.4, 135.6, 133.0, 130.0,
128.8, 128.7, 128.5, 128.5, 128.4, 128.2, 116.1, 111.7, 104.0, 98.6,
67.2, 67.0, 66.4, 55.5, 55.1, 49.4, 45.3, 38.1, 32.0, 30.8, 27.9, 24.1,
22.8, 22.3, 14.9. IR (neat): 3300, 2938, 2837, 1723, 1683, 1614, 1589,
1507, 1455, 1438, 1383, 1287, 1259, 1208, 1158, 1029 cm-1. HRMS (ESI):
calcd for C39H46N3O8 [M + H]+ 684.3285, found 684.3318. Mp: 51 °C. [α]25D
-20.66 (c 0.75, MeOH).
