$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of α-acyloxy-α-cyanoamide 5a: A
homogeneous mixture of pyruvonitrile (4.4 mmol) and acetic acid (4.4
mmol) was stirred for 10 min at 0°C under argon, then cyclohexyl
isonitrile (4 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was warmed to rt and
stirred for 1 h, whereupon any volatile residues were removed in vacuo
(0.1 Torr, 4 h). The crude product was purified by crystallization from
EtOH to afford white needles of 5a (0.57 g, 68%): 5g: The crude product
was purified by silica gel flash column chromatography (3:7
EtOAc/hexanes, Rf = 0.6) to afford clear oil that solidified upon
standing (0.36 g, 75%): mp 52- 55 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.05 (d, 1 H, J =
7.7 Hz), 3.74 (m, 1 H), 2.41 (m, 1 H), 1.9-2.1 (m, 2 H), 1.86 (s, 3 H),
1.6-1.8 (m, 6 H), 1.1-1.4 (m, 13 H), 0.87 (t, 3 H, J = 7 Hz); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 171.63, 163.52, 117.00, 70.27, 49.44, 33.51, 32.52, 32.45,
31.54, 28.84, 28.79, 25.30, 24.64, 24.56, 24.46, 24.20, 22.54, 14.03 ppm;
IR (neat) 3324 (w, br), 2931 (s), 2857 (m), 1762 (s), 1677 (s), 1535 (s),
1450 (m) cm-1; CIMS (methane) m/z: 323 (M+H), 197, 170, 127.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent, Passerini condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
