$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of α-acyloxy-α-cyanoamide 5a: A
homogeneous mixture of pyruvonitrile (4.4 mmol) and acetic acid (4.4
mmol) was stirred for 10 min at 0°C under argon, then cyclohexyl
isonitrile (4 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was warmed to rt and
stirred for 1 h, whereupon any volatile residues were removed in vacuo
(0.1 Torr, 4 h). The crude product was purified by crystallization from
EtOH to afford white needles of 5a (0.57 g, 68%): 5b: The crude product
was purified by crystallization from EtOH/hexanes to afford white plates
(0.57 g, 74%): mp 122-123 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.05 (d, 1 H, J = 7.94
Hz), 3.76 (m, 1 H), 2.17 (s, 3 H), 1.2-2.1 (m, 25 H), 0.88 (t, 3 H, J =
6.9 Hz); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 169.19, 163.31, 116.74, 74.66, 49.76, 37.19,
32.86, 32.70, 31.85, 29.17, 29.12, 25.58, 24.93, 24.84, 23.86, 22.81,
20.62, 14.30 ppm; IR (neat) 3322 (m), 2924 (s), 2859 (m), 1759 (s), 1660
(s), 1545 (m), 1216 (m) cm-1; CIMS (methane) m/z: 323.3 (M+H), 281, 254,
155, 83.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent, Passerini condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Three-Component Condensation Leading to β-Amino Acid Diamides: Convergent
Assembly of β-Peptide Analogues
