$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Formation of Phosphonate 5: To acyl chloride 1
(2 mmol) was added neat trialkyl phosphite (1 equiv). The mixture was
stirred under argon for 30 min. Toluene (1 M), isocyanide (1 equiv) and
carboxylic acid (1 equiv) were then successively added. The mixture was
stirred for 24 h under argon at r.t. (for alkyl acyl chlorides) or at 80
°C (for aromatic acyl chlorides). The solvent was then removed under
reduced pressure to afford Passerini products after purification by flash
column chromatography on silica gel. Compound 5a, yield 74a %. Mp 72-74
°C; Rf (EtOAc-PE, 50:50): 0.1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.26-7.33 (m,
2 H), 7.18-7.24 (m, 3 H), 6.73 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1 H), 3.84-3.88 (m, 1 H),
3.88 (d, JH-P = 10.8 Hz, 3 H), 3.84 (d, JH-P = 10.6 Hz, 3 H), 2.69-2.80
(m, 1 H), 2.56-2.69 (m, 3 H), 2.18 (s, 3 H), 1.91-1.99 (m, 2 H),
1.68-1.78 (m, 2 H), 1.59-1.66 (m, 1 H), 1.33-1.47 (m, 2 H), 1.17-1.32 (m,
3 H). 13C NMR (100.6 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 169.1 (d, JC-P = 5.9 Hz), 165.2 (d,
JC-P = 4.4 Hz), 141.4, 129.0, 128.9, 126.5, 83.3 (d, JC-P = 152.2 Hz),
55.1 (d, JC-P = 6.6 Hz), 54.5 (d, JC-P = 7.3 Hz), 49.1, 35.6, 33.2, 33.1,
30.5 (d, JC-P = 7.3 Hz), 25.9, 25.1, 21.6. IR (thin film): 3328, 3027,
2987, 1749, 1669, 1531, 1259, 1222, 1020 cm-1. HRMS: m/z calcd for
C20H30NO6P: 411.1811; found: 411.1810.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Passerini reaction, neat reactants 1st stage
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isocyanide addition to acylphosphonates: a formal Passerini reaction of
acyl chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Coffinier, Didier; El Kaim, Laurent; Grimaud, Laurence
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2008), (8), 1133-1136

