$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of azetidine-2,3-dione 1 (1 mmol) in anhydrous acetonitrile
(5 mL), the corresponding carboxylic acid (1.05 mmol) and p-methoxyphenyl
isocyanide (PMPNC) (1.10 mmol) were sequentially added, at room
temperature and under argon atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred
at reflux temperature for 12 h. Then, a second equivalent of PMPNC was
added and the resulting mixture was stirred at reflux temperature until
complete disappearance of the starting material (TLC). After that, the
resulting reaction mixture was worked-up as indicated above (Method B).
Passerini Adduct (+)-2m. Method C. From 45 mg (0.15 mmol) of
azetidine-2,3-dione (+)-1a, 61 mg (74%) of compound (+)-2m was obtained
as a colorless oil after purification by flash chromatography
(hexanes/ethyl acetate, 1:1). [α]D = +25.6 (c 0.3, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3, 25 °C) δ 8.16 (bs, 1H), 8.09-8.06 (m, 2H), 7.64 (m, 2H),
7.67-7.63 (m, 1H), 7.54-7.49 (m, 2H), 7.44 (m, 2H), 6.93m, 2H), 6.84 (m,
2H), 4.94 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 4.55 (q, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 4.20 (dd, J =
8.9, 6.7 Hz, 1H), 4.11 (dd, J = 8.8, 6.9 Hz, 1H), 3.82 and 3.78 (s, each
3H), 1.50 and 1.31 (s, each 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, 25 °C) δ 164.5,
162.0, 160.2, 157.2, 157.1, 134.3, 130.2, 130.1, 129.8, 128.8, 127.9,
122.1, 120.6, 114.2, 114.1, 110.3, 86.5, 75.4, 66.9, 64.4, 55.5, 55.4,
26.5, 25.2; IR (CHCl3, cm-1) υ 3309, 1753, 1687; HRMS (ESI) for
C30H31N2O8+ (M + H)+ calcd 547.2075, found 547.2097.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
