$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Acyloxy-3-chlorocarboxamides 4; General
Procedure: α-Chloro ketone 1 (10 mmol) is added dropwise over 15 min to
an ice-cooled mixture of carboxylic acid 2 (10 mmol) and isocyanide 3 (10
mmol). The mixture is stirred for 15 h at room temperature. The resulting
product is purified by distillation or by crystallisation from petroleum
ether. 2-Acyloxy-3-chloropropanamide 4e. Yield: 73%. m.p.: 139 [°C],
Molecular Formula: C17H22ClNO3 (323.8). Microanalyses: C, ± 0.23; H, ±
0.19; N, ± 0.47: Cl, ± 0.40. I.R. (Nujol) ν[cm-1]: 1620; 1654; 1706;
3370. 1H-N.M.R. (CDCl3/TMSint) δ [ppm]: 1.41 (s, 9H); 1.75 (s, 3H); 4.14,
4.31 (νA, νB, 2H, JAB= 12 Hz); 6.22 (br. s, 1H, NH); 6.43 (d, 1 H, Jtrans
= 16 Hz); 7.4 (m, 5 Harom): 7.70 (d, 1 H, Jtrans = 16 Hz).
