$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Phenol-Induced Ugi-4CR.
To a 1 M solution of the aldehyde (1 mmol) in methanol was added
successively 1.0 equiv of amine, 1.0 equiv of isocyanide, and 1.0 equiv
of phenol under inert atmosphere. The resulting mixture was stirred until
completion (TLC). It was then concentrated in vacuo, and the crude
product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
2-(N-allyl-N-(2-nitro phenyl)amino)-N-cyclohexyl butanamideYellow oil.
Yield (16h at 60°C in MeOH): 72%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.71 (dd, 1H,
J = 8.1, 1.4 Hz), 7.49 (td, 1H, J = 7.8, 1.4 Hz), 7.28 (dd, 1H, J = 7.8,
1.0 Hz), 7.16 (td, 1H, J = 7.8, 1.0 Hz), 6.96 (d, 1H, J = 8.1 Hz), 5.65
(dddd, 1H, J = 16.9, 10.3, 6.4, 4.3 Hz), 5.09 (dd, 1H, J = 10.3, 1.1 Hz),
5.08 (dd, 1H, J = 16.9, 1.1 Hz), 3.81-3.69 (m, 3H), 3.53 (dd, 1H, J =
15.5, 6.4 Hz), 2.02-1.91 (m, 1H), 1.91-1.83 (m, 1H), 1.78-1.54 (m, 4H),
1.42-1.02 (m, 6H), 0.93 (t, 3H, J = 7.3 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100.6 MHz) δ
170.8, 146.3, 143.1, 133.2, 133.0, 125.6, 124.1, 119.6, 68.5, 53.7, 48.2,
33.4, 33.0, 25.9, 25.2, 23.5, 11.4. IR (thin film) 3384, 2932, 2856,
1664, 1523, 1159 cm-1. MS (DI, CI NH3) m/z 345. HRMS Calcd. for
C19H27N3O3 345.2052, Found 345.2066.
