$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Compounds 3 and 8 A solution of 0.166 g (1 mmol) triethyl phosphite in 5
mL CH2Cl2 was added dropwise to a magnetically stirred solution of acyl
chloride 2 (1 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (5 mL) at 0 °C over 15 min. The mixture
was then allowed to warm to r.t. and stirred for 30 min. Benzoic acid 7
(1 mmol) and isocyanide 5 (1 mmol) were then added. The mixture was
stirred for 24 h (60 h for 3e, 3f and 3g) at r.t. The solvent was removed
under reduced pressure and the residue was purified by layer
chromatography on silica gel (SiO2, petroleum ether/ethyl acetate 10:2)
to afford the pure compounds. The characterization data of compounds 8
are given below. 1-(N-Cyclohexylcarbamoyl)-1-(diethoxyphosphoryl)ethyl
benzoate (8a). 1-(N-tert-Butylcarbamoyl)-1-(diethoxyphosphoryl)ethyl
4-methylbenzoate (8c). Colorless viscous oil, yield: 70%. IR (νmax,
cm−1): 3436 (NH), 2922, 1732(C=O), 1688(C=O), 1524, 1455, 1268 (P=O),
1027. 1H NMR: δ 1.28-1.42 (m, 6H, 2CH3CH2OPO), 1.32 (s, 9H, me3C), 1.92
(d, 3H, 3JHP=15.5 Hz, CH3), 2.42 (s, 3H, me), 4.15-4.40 (m, 4H, 2CH2OPO),
6.24 (s, NH), 7.26 (d, 2 H, 3JHH=8.0 Hz, arom), 7.93 (d, 2 H, 3JHH =8.0
Hz, arom). 13C NMR: δ 16.4 (d, 3JCP =5.7 Hz, CH3CH2OPO), 16.5 (d, 3JCP
=5.7 Hz, CH3CH2OPO), 17.8 (d, 2JCP=2.5 Hz, CH3), 21.7 (Me), 30.9 (Me3C),
51.6 (Me3C), 63.9 (d, 2JCP =5.7 Hz, CH2OPO), 64.0 (d, 2JCP=6.3 Hz,
CH2OPO), 80.8 (d, 1JCP=160.4 Hz, C), 126.9, 129.2, 129.9, 144.3, 164.1
(d, 3JCP=12.8 Hz, C=O ester), 165.3 (d, 2JCP=2.1 Hz, C=O amide). 31P NMR:
δ 19.1. Anal. Calcd. for C19H30NO6P (399.43): C 57.13, H 7.57, N 3.51,
found C 57.46, H 7.76, N 3.74%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM dropwise addn. of phosphite (stage 1, substage 1), Passerini reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of α-Ketophosphonate Derivatives and Their Application in the
Synthesis of 1-(N-Alkylcarbamoyl)-1-(diethoxyphosphoryl)alkyl Benzoates
via Passerini Reaction
