$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Phenol-Induced Ugi-4CR.
To a 1 M solution of the aldehyde (1 mmol) in methanol was added
successively 1.0 equiv of amine, 1.0 equiv of isocyanide, and 1.0 equiv
of phenol under inert atmosphere. The resulting mixture was stirred until
completion (TLC). It was then concentrated in vacuo, and the crude
product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
2-(N-(4-chloro benzyl)-N-(2-nitro
phenyl)amino)-N-cyclohexyl-2-(3-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl) acetamide.Yellow
solid. Yield (20h at 60°C in MeOH): 70%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.73
(br s, 1H), 7.67 (dd, 1H, J = 8.1, 1.5 Hz), 7.60 (d, 1H, J = 7.6 Hz),
7.52 (t, 1H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.40 (dd, 1H, J = 7.8, 1.5 Hz), 7.29-7.22 (m,
3H), 7.19-7.15 (m, 2H), 6.99 (dd, 1H, J = 8.1, 1.5 Hz), 6.69-6.65 (m,
2H), 4.90 (s, 1H), 4.04 (d, 1H, J = 14.1 Hz), 3.92 (d, 1H, J = 14.1 Hz),
3.63-3.53 (m, 1H), 1.82-1.44 (m, 6H), 1.29- 1.05 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (CDCl3,
100.6 MHz) δ 168.7, 147.8, 141.7, 137.5, 134.8, 133.1, 132.9, 132.9,
131.2, 129.8, 127.3, 126.4, 126.0, 125.1, 71.7, 57.3, 48.3, 32.8, 25.7,
25.0, 24.9. IR (thin film) 3321, 2936, 2855, 1662, 1525, 1328, 1168, 1131
cm-1. MS (DI, CI NH3) m/z 547. HRMS Calcd. for C28H27ClF3N3O3 545.1693,
Found 545.1673. m.p. 101°C.
