$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure B (CH2Cl2 solvent): Synthesis of
α-acyloxy-α-cyanocarboxamides 5f, 5i, 5j, 5m, 5n,5p, 5r, 5u, 5x.
Synthesis of α-acyloxy-α-cyanoamide 5f: To a stirred solution of
pyruvonitrile(115 μL, 1.6 mmol) and trans-cinnamic acid (0.24 g,1.6 mmol)
in CH2Cl2 (4 mL) at 0°C under argon was added cyclohexyl isonitrile (190
μL, 1.4 mmol). The reaction mixture was warmed to rt and stirred for 12
h, CH2Cl2 (5 mL), then saturated NaHCO3 (5 mL) was added. The layers were
separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 5 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with brine (5 mL) and dried with
MgSO4. The solvent was evaporated and the residue was purified by
crystallization from EtOH/hexanes to afford white needles of 5f (0.24 g,
50%): 5n: The crude product was purified by silica gel flash column
chromatography (1:4 EtOAc/hexanes, Rf = 0.26) to afford two diastereomers
as a white solid (0.88 g, 70%): mp 51°C; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.27-7.37 (m, 3
H), 7.18-7.23 (m, 2 H), 6.32/6.59 (s, 1 H), 4.84/4.97 (d, 1 H, J = 6.4
Hz), 4.29/4.46 (q, 1 H, J = 6.5 Hz), 3.12 (m, 2 H), 1.74/1.79 (s, 3 H),
1.40/1.42 (s, 9 H), 1.35/1.36 (2s, 9 H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 169.52,
169.48, 163.54, 163.46, 155.91, 155.47, 135.38, 134.73, 129.56, 129.52,
129.35, 129.25, 129.16, 129.05, 128.92, 128.69, 127.67, 127.40, 116.01,
115.91, 80.78, 80.65, 72.85, 72.68, 55.28, 55.20, 54.77, 52.41, 52.36,
36.97, 28.24, 28.17, 28.13, 28.08, 24.67, 24.60 ppm; IR (neat) 3316 (w),
3031 (w), 2977 (M), 1762 (W), 1689 (s), 1527 (s), 1168 (s), 1087 (m)
cm-1; CIMS (methane) m/z: 418 (M+H), 362, 318, 201, 120.
