$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Passerini 3CR: The
aldehyde (0.125 mmol, 1eq.), Isocyanide (0.25 mmol, 2eq.) and carboxylic
acid (0.125 mmol, 1eq.) were added to 125 μL of the solvent in a 1/2 dram
glass vial and stirred overnight. After removal of solvent in vacuo, the
reaction products were purified by flash column chromatography. In
reactions where an alcohol was included, 2eq. of the alcohol were added
along with the substrates at the beginning of the reaction. 3c3 (Table
2)4c3 (Table 2) Flash Chromatography conditions: CH2Cl2 until isocyanide
and aldehyde eluted then 25:1 (CH2Cl2: ethyl acetate). 1H NMR (400MHz;
CDCl3): δ 7.63-7.58 (m, 2H), 7.49-7.47 (m, 2H), 7.44-7.30 (m, 7H), 6.67
(br, 1H), 6.61 (d, J = 3.3, 1H), 6.43-6.41 (m, 1H), 6.40 (s, 1H),
4.70-4.64 (m, 1H), 4.58-4.52 (m, 1H). LRMS: calcd 359.37 for C22H17NO4,
observed 382.1 [M + Na]+.1H NMR (400MHz; CDCl3): δ 7.43-7.13 (m, 17H),
6.56-6.54 (m, 1H), 6.23 (dd, J = 3.4, 1.9, 1H), 6.17 (s, 1H), 5.12 (d, J
= 16.8, 1H), 4.94 (d, J = 16.7, 1H), 4.50 (dd, J = 15.0, 6.0, 1H), 4.34
(dd, J = 15.0, 5.6, 1H). 13C NMR (100MHz; CDCl3): δ 166.9, 156.1, 147.0,
143.1, 137.7, 136.9, 132.5, 130.3, 128.7, 128.5, 128.2, 127.6, 127.5,
126.8, 120.0, 112.5, 110.8, 104.4, 91.7, 81.7, 55.6, 51.6, 43.7. LRMS:
calcd 448.51 for C29H24N2O3, observed 471.2 [M + Na]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bronsted Acidity of Substrates Influences the Outcome of Passerini
Three-Component Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Okandeji, Babajide O.; Sello, Jason K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
