$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Passerini 3CR: The
aldehyde (0.125 mmol, 1eq.), Isocyanide (0.25 mmol, 2eq.) and carboxylic
acid (0.125 mmol, 1eq.) were added to 125 μL of the solvent in a 1/2 dram
glass vial and stirred overnight. After removal of solvent in vacuo, the
reaction products were purified by flash column chromatography. In
reactions where an alcohol was included, 2eq. of the alcohol were added
along with the substrates at the beginning of the reaction. 3a (Table
2)4a (Table 2) Flash Chromatography conditions: CH2Cl2 until isocyanide
and aldehyde eluted then 80:1 (CH2Cl2: ethyl acetate). 1H NMR (400MHz;
CDCl3): δ 7.63-7.61 (m, 2H), 7.50 (t, J = 7.5, 1H), 7.41 (t, J = 7.5,
2H), 7.36 (d, J = 6.5, 2H), 7.32 (d, J = 7.1, 3H), 6.48 (br, 1H), 5.32
(d, J = 4.2, 1H), 4.61 (dd, J = 14.9, 6.2, 1H), 4.46 (dd, J = 14.9, 5.6,
1H), 2.47-2.42 (m, 1H), 1.07 (t, J = 6.7, 6H). 13C NMR (100MHz; CDCl3): δ
168.6, 152.9, 137.8, 133.1, 131.1, 128.8, 128.7, 127.8, 127.7, 119.1,
88.4, 79.9, 79.6, 43.2, 30.9, 18.8, 17.0. HRMS: calcd 358.1419 for
C21H21NNaO3 ([M + Na]+), observed 358.1419.1H NMR (400MHz; CDCl3): δ
7.46-7.32 (m, 13H), 7.24-7.22 (m, 2H), 6.96 (br, 1H), 5.07 (d, J = 16.0,
1H), 4.85 (d, J = 16.0, 1H), 4.38 (dd, 14.9, 5.9, 1H), 4.25 (d, J = 11.8,
1H), 4.21 (dd, J = 14.9, 5.6, 1H), 2.62-2.56 (m, 1H), 0.96 (d, J = 6.5,
3H), 0.73 (d, J = 6.6, 3H). 13C NMR (100MHz; CDCl3): δ 169.4, 156.6,
138.1, 136.9, 132.5, 130.4, 128.64, 128.57, 128.53, 127.9, 127.73,
127.68, 127.3, 120.0, 92.0, 82.1, 43.4, 27.0, 19.9, 19.1.HRMS: calcd
447.2048 for C28H28N2O2+Na, observed 447.2045 [M + Na]+.
